  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Access to and experiences with reproductive health care for LGBTQ+ people. Reproductive health care includes birth control, abortion, assisted reproduction, and prenatal and obstetric care.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Access to and experiences with reproductive health care for non-binary people. Reproductive health care includes birth control, abortion, assisted reproduction, and prenatal and obstetric care.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Access to and experiences with reproductive health care for transgender people. Reproductive health care includes birth control, abortion, assisted reproduction, and prenatal and obstetric care.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">People who are pregnant, meaning that a fertilized egg is developing in their uterus.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The termination of a pregnancy.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Term used to describe the various aspects determining whether abortions are accessible to LGBTQ+ people in a given location. Factors determining accessibility include legality, safety, privacy, financial cost, freedom of travel, etc.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">An individual's right to make informed decisions about their own body without external influence or coercion.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Access to and experiences with reproductive health care for Two-Spirit people. Reproductive health care includes birth control, abortion, assisted reproduction, and prenatal and obstetric care.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Legal, social, or ethical principles of freedom around reproductive healthcare and decision-making. Often used to refer to an individual's right to bodily autonomy and access to legal and safe birth control, abortion, assisted reproduction, and prenatal and obstetric care.</subfield>
  </datafield>
